---
# Create Application

The Application class is the entry point and nothing more. It boots the JRebirth runtime, configures the shell (stage, scene, global CSS), and hands control to the first Model. All feature logic lives elsewhere.

## What belongs here

- Bootstrap and launch flow (`preloadAndLaunch(args)` in `main`).
- The choice of the first Model class, returned by `firstModelClass()`.
- Stage title and window icon configuration.
- Scene customization and global CSS stylesheets.
- The list of resources to preload before the UI appears.

## What does not belong here

- Business logic of any kind.
- Feature orchestration or state management.
- Controller-style event handling.
- Direct backend or service access.

If you find yourself adding any of these, move them to the appropriate role (Model, Command, or Service).

## Key API

- Extend `DefaultApplication<StackPane>` (or whichever root pane type the shell uses).
- Return the first Model class from `firstModelClass()`.
- Set the window title in `applicationTitle()`.
- Add global stylesheets in `customizeScene(scene)` with `addCSS(scene, SomeStyles.DEFAULT)`.
- Tune the window in `customizeStage(stage)`.
- List resources to preload in `getResourceToPreload()`.

Template: `templates/ApplicationTemplate.java.txt`.
